.DS_Store
# Hooks registered on this machine only. `scripts/precommit.py` runs what is in
# here alongside the tracked hooks in `hooks.d/`, and nothing here is meant to be
# staged, so a check kept outside this repository can join the run without this
# repository disclosing that it exists. Anchored to the root so a crate's own
# `.clio-hooks` directory stays trackable.
/.clio-hooks/
# The store's own artifacts. `*.lock` is the cross-process store lock; the
# other three suffixes are the sidecars SQLite creates beside a database file.
# A rollback journal holds original page images, so its bytes are store content
# and must not be stageable. These follow the same three extensions the lock
# patterns above cover, so a store pointed inside the checkout is covered
# whichever of them it uses.
*.db.lock
*.sqlite.lock
*.sqlite3.lock
*.db-journal
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.sqlite-journal
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm
*.sqlite3-journal
*.sqlite3-wal
*.sqlite3-shm
